WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.560
Five numbers. One pyramid.

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:03.540
How large can we make the top?

00:00:04.116 --> 00:00:05.976
Place one to five along the bottom.

00:00:06.616 --> 00:00:09.496
Each box adds the three closest boxes below it.

00:00:09.972 --> 00:00:11.032
Follow the centre number.

00:00:11.432 --> 00:00:13.012
It appears in all three middle sums.

00:00:13.617 --> 00:00:15.157
So it reaches the top three times.

00:00:15.816 --> 00:00:16.856
The neighbours count twice.

00:00:17.536 --> 00:00:18.796
Each end counts only once.

00:00:19.449 --> 00:00:22.229
Put five in the centre, three and four beside it, and

00:00:22.229 --> 00:00:23.289
one and two at the ends.

00:00:23.942 --> 00:00:26.902
A larger number earns more in a position that counts more.

00:00:27.522 --> 00:00:29.102
That is why this arrangement is best.

00:00:29.792 --> 00:00:31.972
The middle row becomes nine, twelve and eleven.

00:00:32.712 --> 00:00:33.492
Add them: thirty-two.

00:00:34.335 --> 00:00:37.015
Answer C. Count how often each number contributes.

